did auxiliary.","B":"The negative past-simple clause takes the positive tag **did they**.","C":"The main clause is already negative; the ordinary checking tag is positive.","D":"Do changes the tense to present."}}},{"id":"d87ddd7a-3afa-54ba-a2c5-05727ffa8264","topicSlug":"question-tags","level":"B1","prompt":"“We are preparing the evening meal, ____?”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"aren’t we"},{"id":"B","text":"don’t we"},{"id":"C","text":"isn’t we"},{"id":"D","text":"weren’t we"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The statement already contains **are**; keep that auxiliary family.","explanation":"Reuse **are** and the pronoun we, with negative polarity.","keywords":["continuous-tag"],"skill":"continuous-tag","contextKey":"question-tags-49","fingerprint":"d255b2ecca4a94459e7fb0d92e5add3883286e4a5aa2dbd24b05029fa54103ce","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-question-tags"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The statement already contains **are**; keep that auxiliary family.","Reuse **are** and the pronoun we, with negative polarity.","Choose **aren’t we**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Reuse **are** and the pronoun we, with negative polarity.","B":"The existing auxiliary is are, not do.","C":"Is does not agree with we.","D":"Were changes the time to past."}}},{"id":"eba3305f-58a7-5ec5-a539-496c2681a4db","topicSlug":"question-tags","level":"B1","prompt":"“Let’s prepare the evening meal, ____?”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"do we"},{"id":"B","text":"aren’t we"},{"id":"C","text":"did we"},{"id":"D","text":"shall we"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Recognise the special **let’s … shall we?** pattern.","explanation":"The usual tag after a shared suggestion with **let’s** is **shall we**.","keywords":["suggestion-tag"],"skill":"suggestion-tag","contextKey":"question-tags-49","fingerprint":"e693